# ── OD-Amrita monorepo .gitignore ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Reconciliation note (Story 1.1): the previous root .gitignore blanket-ignored
# `Makefile`, which would hide the legitimate surface Makefiles. Surface build
# files (contracts/Makefile, api/Makefile) are TRACKED; only tooling/output and
# secrets are ignored below.

# ── Secrets & local env ──
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# ── IDE & editor ──
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# ── Node / JS ──
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
# pnpm puts its store on the same filesystem as the project, so it normally lands
# outside the repo — but not always (a container whose checkout sits on its own
# overlay resolves it to the repo root instead). Untracked, it fails the
# contract-drift gate, whose final check is `git status --porcelain` over the
# WHOLE repo and reports any stray path as "generated output drifted".
.pnpm-store/
dist/
build/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/
tmp/

# ── Go ──
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.test
*.out
/bin/
api/bin/

# ── Mobile (Expo / RN) ──
mobile/.expo/
mobile/android/
mobile/ios/
mobile/*.log

# ── BMAD / agent tooling & private working dirs (not product code) ──
.agent/
.agents/
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
_bmad/
_bmad-logs/
_bmad-output/
bmad-logs/
mydocs/
response-output/
base-idea.txt
# Local Claude Code / GSD agent-orchestration setup notes — tooling, not product.
SETUP-GUIDE.md

AGENTS.md

# Private operations notes (kept locally)
# Deployment-specific runbooks and records. The generic, publishable version is
# docs/deployment.md.
docs/auth-microsoft-supabase-setup.md
docs/deploy-walkthrough.md
docs/deployment-runbook.md
docs/backup-and-monitoring-runbook.md
docs/cost-and-latency-record.md
docs/Amrita-OD_Neon_Monitoring_Cleaned.md
docs/event-stream-record.md
docs/admin-portal-operations.md
# Local act (nektos/act) defaults. api/scripts/ci_local.sh passes the safety
# flags itself, so the repository does not depend on this file.
/.actrc

sprint-status.yaml

# ── Superseded application, kept locally for reference only ──
# MUST NEVER reach GitHub. Local-only working copy; not product code and not a
# build input. Both spellings are ignored so a rename cannot quietly un-ignore it.
old-od-app/
old-od-app

# Vercel CLI project linkage. Local-only: it names the project a machine is
# linked to, and committing it makes every clone deploy to whatever project the
# last person happened to be linked to.
.vercel/

# ── Local roster and attendance exports ──
# Source data belongs in the database or an approved private store, never Git.
/*.csv
/*.xls
/*.xlsx
